      "httpStatus": 200,
      "latencyMs": 1184,
      "answer": "The Malthusian trap is the classical idea that any increase in food or income gets wiped out by population growth, so living standards stay stuck near subsistence. Because land is limited, adding more workers leads to diminishing returns, and output per person falls back down. In this view, prosperity cannot last unless something breaks the cycle of population rising faster than production.",
